    "text": "(Well-known problem). By a famous theorem of Wielandt the sequence G0 =\nG, G1 , . . ., where Gi+1 = Aut Gi , stabilizes for any finite group G with trivial centre.\nDoes there exist a function f of natural argument such that |Gi | ⩽ f (|G|) for all i =\n0, 1, . . . for an arbitrary finite group G and the same kind of sequence? V. D. Mazurov",
